WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
So this lesson compares grinders using the notebook from our first coffee practice. Keep the recipe nearby.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Um, begin with the same dose of coffee and the same paper filter. We want a fair comparison.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Our grind size is the first adjustment today. Mark the current setting before moving the adjustment ring.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
A finer grind size exposes more surface and may slow drainage. Smaller steps make comparisons easier to understand.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The sour coffee question from our first lesson has a practical answer. Try grinding a little finer first.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
A finer setting can increase extraction and reduce sharp sour taste. Compare the cups before changing anything else.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Use the same water amount in each cup. An extra splash could hide the difference we are trying to observe.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
The grind size should be easy to repeat. A marked dial helps us return to a setting that tasted good.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
You know, the dial numbers are only reference marks. Matching numbers on different grinders does not guarantee matching particles.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
And so grind size belongs in our notebook beside time and taste. Record each adjustment before brewing again.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
What cleaning interval keeps a grinder consistent with daily use? We have not measured that interval in these lessons.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Some grinders retain a small amount of ground coffee inside. Tap gently and check the instructions for safe cleaning.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Like, sound alone does not tell us the particle size. Compare the brewed cups instead of guessing from noise.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Keep the water temperature similar during the comparison. We are changing the grinder setting while holding other choices steady.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Our second cup now tastes less sharp than the first. Record that observation without calling it a universal rule.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.000
A coarse grind size can still suit another recipe. The best setting here belongs to this particular practice session.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Turn the adjustment ring only as the equipment instructions allow. Stop if it resists and check those instructions again.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.000
We will leave the grinder on the chosen setting today. Repeating the recipe tomorrow tests whether the result holds.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.000
We'll talk about water next time. The liquid itself deserves a comparison after these first grinder adjustments.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Write down the amount poured and the final cup weight. These notes let us repeat our own small experiment.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Check the table for scattered grounds before putting things away. Brush them into the bin with the power disconnected.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Our notebook now contains two useful cups and one adjustment. Bring those notes to the next tasting session.
